      "message": "fix(post): no per-user assets folder; dev fallbacks only in a cargo tree\n\nReview of PR #2293:\n- Remove the per-user `<data>/camcraft/assets/<kind>` candidate. It came\n  before the dev candidates, so a stale copy could replace the repository\n  scripts for `cargo run` and the golden tests with no warning.\n- Use `<exe>/../../assets` and the compiled-in CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR only\n  when the exe is in a cargo build tree (cargo's `.fingerprint` folder in\n  the profile folder). An installed exe without `assets/<kind>` gets the\n  named refusal, never the build machine's checkout or /usr/assets.\n- Pin the 4 MiB cap and the wasm32 `embedded()` list against the tables.\n- Restore the two import_step_guard test files that changed only in\n  line endings.\n\nFixes #2282\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
